-- T6 regression: a failed re-force of a demoted WHNFWhen cache must not
-- permanently poison the thunk.
--
-- 'evalRef' demotes a stale WHNFWhen cache to a blackholed Unevaluated
-- before re-forcing it under the current context. Pre-fix, when that
-- re-force raised an exception the unwind dropped the UpdateThunk frame
-- without restoring the thunk, leaving it blackholed forever: every later
-- force — including under the ORIGINAL, still-valid context — reported
-- "Infinite loop detected". Fixed by restoring the displaced cache during
-- exceptional unwinding ('restoreThunkOnUnwind' in Machine.hs); directive 3
-- then serves the still-fingerprint-valid cache produced by directive 1.
--
-- The test harness pins the clock: JL4_FIXED_NOW = 2025-01-31T15:45:30Z,
-- so the ambient serial difference below is 1857 days (and 0 days under
-- AS OF SYSTEM TIME 2020-01-01).

TIMEZONE IS "Etc/UTC"

x MEANS 1 DIVIDED BY (DATE_SERIAL TODAY MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020))

-- expected: 0.0005385029617662897 (= 1/1857; cached as WHNFWhen)
#EVAL x

-- expected: Division by zero (the demoted cache's re-force fails under the
-- override)
#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020)) x

-- expected: 0.0005385029617662897 again, served from the restored cache
-- (pre-fix: "Infinite loop detected")
#EVAL x

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A fresh (never-cached) thunk whose first force fails must also stay
-- re-forcible: the aborted force clears its blackhole mark on unwind.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

y MEANS 1 DIVIDED BY (DATE_SERIAL TODAY MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020))

-- expected: Division by zero, twice (pre-fix the second directive reported
-- "Infinite loop detected" off the leftover blackhole mark)
#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020)) y
#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020)) y

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Genuine self-reference must STILL be detected as an infinite loop: the
-- unwind-time restore must not defeat same-thread blackhole detection.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

r MEANS DATE_SERIAL TODAY PLUS r

-- expected: Infinite loop detected (in both directives)
#EVAL r
#EVAL r
